          %p
            In
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/string+theory"} string theory
            %em Hanany-Witten-effect
            (or
            = succeed "," do
              %em -process
            = succeed "," do
              %em -tansition
            = succeed ")" do
              %em -move
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/type+II+string+theory"} type II string theory
            which is roughly described as follows:
          %p
            “
            %em>
              Moving an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/NS5-brane"} NS5-brane
              across a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D-brane"}
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi D
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn 2
                      %mi p
                      %mo +
                      %mi σ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D (2p+\sigma)
                \-brane
              creates a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D-brane"}
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi D
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn 2
                      %mi p
                      %mo −
                      %mn 2
                      %mo +
                      %mi σ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D (2p-2 + \sigma)
                \-brane
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/intersecting+branes"} stretching between
              the two
            ”.
          %blockquote
            %p
              (Here
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi σ
                    %mo =
                    %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sigma = 0
              in
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/type+IIA+string+theory"} type IIA string theory
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi σ
                    %mo =
                    %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sigma=1
              in
              = succeed ".)" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/type+IIB+string+theory"} type IIB string theory
          %p
            Something like this was informally argued in
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#HananyWitten97"} Hanany &amp; Witten (1997)
          %p
            %a{:href => "#NakatsuEtAl98"}> Nakatsu et al (1998)
            \:
          %center
            %div{:style => "margin:-40px 10px 10px 0;"}
              %img{:src => "/nlab/files/NakatsuEtAl-HananyWittenEffect.jpg", :width => "680"}/
              %img/
          %p
            %a{:href => "#Marolf01"}> Marolf (2001)
            \:
          %center
            %div{:style => "margin:-40px 10px 10px 0;"}
              %img{:src => "/nlab/files/Marolf-HananyWittenEffect.jpg", :width => "440"}/
              %img/
          %p
            %a{:href => "#EtoEtAl05"}> Eto et al (2005)
            \:
          %center
            %div{:style => "margin:-40px 10px 10px 0;"}
              %img{:src => "/nlab/files/EtoEtAl-HananyWittenEffect.jpg", :width => "720"}/
              %img/
          %p
            %a{:href => "#Pelc08"}> Pelc (2008)
            \:
          %center
            %div{:style => "margin:-40px 10px 10px 0;"}
              %img{:src => "/nlab/files/Pelc-HananyWittenEffect.jpg", :width => "480"}/
              %img/
          %p
            %a{:href => "#GangEtAl11"}> Gang et al (2011)
            \:
          %center
            %div{:style => "margin:-40px 10px 10px 0;"}
              %img{:src => "/nlab/files/GangEtAl-HananyWittenEffect.jpg", :width => "600"}/
              %img/
          %p
            %br/
          %p
            %a{:href => "#Marolf01"} Marolf (2001)
            suggested that the Hanany-Witten effect may be understood entirely as a consequence of the famous (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pregeometric+RR-field"}> pregeometric
            )
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Bianchi+identity"} Bianchi identity
            for the
            = succeed "-" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/RR-field"} RR-field
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fluxes"} fluxes
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi F
                    %mrow
                      %mn 8
                      %mo −
                      %mn 2
                      %mi p
                      %mo −
                      %mi σ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F_{8-2p-\sigma}
            sourced by the
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D-branes"} D-branes
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/twisted+de+Rham+cohomology"} twisted
            by the
            = succeed "-" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/B-field"} B-field
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/flux"} flux
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi H
                    %mn 3
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H_3
            sourced by
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/NS5-branes"} NS5-branes
          #eq:GeneralBianchiIdentity.maruku-equation
            %span.maruku-eq-number (1)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} d
                  %msub
                    %mi F
                    %mrow
                      %mn 8
                      %mo −
                      %mn 2
                      %mi p
                      %mo −
                      %mi σ
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo =
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %msub
                    %mi H
                    %mn 3
                  %mo ∧
                  %msub
                    %mi F
                    %mrow
                      %mn 8
                      %mo −
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn 2
                      %mi p
                      %mo +
                      %mn 2
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo −
                      %mi σ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\mathrm{d}
                  F_{8-2p-\sigma}
                  \\;=\;
                  H_3 \wedge F_{8-(2p+2)-\sigma}
          %p
            and offered an argument in prose &amp;lbrack;
            %a{:href => "#Marolf01"}> Marolf (2001) pp. 3
            \&amp;rbrack;.
          %p
            %a{:href => "#Examples"} Below
            we spell out this approach in more detail.
          %h2#Examples Examples
          %h3#D6StretchingBetweenNS5AndD8 D6 stretching between D8 and NS5
          %p
            (cf.
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D6-D8+brane+bound+state"} D6-D8 brane bound state
            and
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "#BergshoeffLozanoOrtin98"} Bergshoeff, Lozano &amp; Ortin (1998)
          %p
            We explain the “Hanany-Witten effect” in detail for the case of “flat”
            = succeed "\u2013" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/NS5-brane"} NS5
            = succeed "\u2013" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D6-brane"} D6
            = succeed "-configurations," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D8-brane"} D8
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pregeometric+RR-field"} pregeometric
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Bianchi+identities"} Bianchi identities
            %a.maruku-eqref{:href => "#eq:GeneralBianchiIdentity"} (1)
            satisfied by the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/flux+densities"} flux densities
            sourced by these branes.
          %p In this case we are dealing with
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Minkowski+spacetimes"} Minkowski spacetimes
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \;
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi ℝ
                        %mrow
                          %mn 1
                          %mo ,
                          %mi p
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}^{1,p}
                which we may identify with their canonical
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coordinate+charts"} coordinate charts
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msup
                          %mi x
                          %mn 0
                        %mo ,
                        %mover
                          %mi x
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} →
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                        %mo ≔
                        %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msup
                          %mi x
                          %mn 0
                        %mo ,
                        %msup
                          %mi x
                          %mn 1
                        %mo ,
                        %mi ⋯
                        %mo ,
                        %msup
                          %mi x
                          %mi p
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (x^0, \vec x) \,\coloneqq\, (x^0, x^1, \cdots, x^p)
            %li
              %p
                A closed
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+3-form"} differential 3-form
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi H
                        %mn 3
                      %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                      %mo ≔
                      %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                      %mi k
                      %msub
                        %mi vol
                        %mrow
                          %msup
                            %mi S
                            %mn 3
                      %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                      %mo ∈
                      %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                      %msubsup
                        %mi Ω
                        %mi dR
                        %mn 3
                      %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                      %msup
                        %mi S
                        %mn 3
                      %msub
                        %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                        %mi cl
                      %mover
                        %mo →
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %msub
                            %mi pr
                            %mrow
                              %msup
                                %mi S
                                %mn 3
                          %msup
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo *
                      %msubsup
                        %mi Ω
                        %mi dR
                        %mn 3
                      %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                      %msup
                        %mi ℝ
                        %mrow
                          %mn 1
                          %mo ,
                          %mn 5
                      %mo ×
                      %msub
                        %mi ℝ
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} +
                      %mo ×
                      %msup
                        %mi S
                        %mn 3
                      %msub
                        %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                        %mi cl
                      %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                      %mo ≃
                      %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                      %msubsup
                        %mi Ω
                        %mi dR
                        %mn 3
                      %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                      %msup
                        %mi ℝ
                        %mrow
                          %mn 1
                          %mo ,
                          %mn 9
                      %mo ∖
                      %msup
                        %mi ℝ
                        %mrow
                          %mn 1
                          %mo ,
                          %mn 5
                      %msub
                        %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                        %mi cl
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                      H_3
                      \\,\coloneqq\,
                      k vol_{S^3}
                      \\,\in\,
                      \\Omega^3_{dR}\big(
                      S^3
                      \\big)_{cl}
                      \\xrightarrow{(pr_{S^3})^\ast}
                      \\Omega^3_{dR}
                      \\big(
                      \\mathbb{R}^{1,5}
                      \\times
                      \\mathbb{R}_{+}
                      \\times
                      S^3
                      \\big)_{cl}
                      \\,\simeq\,
                      \\Omega^3_{dR}
                      \\big(
                      \\mathbb{R}^{1,9}
                      \\setminus
                      \\mathbb{R}^{1,5}
                      \\big)_{cl}
              %p
                being the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/B-field"} B-field
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/flux+density"} flux density
                sourced by an
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/NS5-brane"} NS5-brane
                with worldvolume
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi ℝ
                        %mrow
                          %mn 5
                          %mo ,
                          %mn 1
                      %mover
                        %mo ↪
                        %mrow
                          %mover
                            %mi x
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} →
                          %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                          %mo ↦
                          %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mover
                            %mi x
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} →
                          %mo ,
                          %mover
                            %mn 0
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} →
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %msup
                        %mi ℝ
                        %mrow
                          %mn 9
                          %mo ,
                          %mn 1
                      %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                      %mo .
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                      \\mathbb{R}^{5,1}
                      \\xhookrightarrow{
                      \\vec x \,\mapsto\, (\vec x, \vec 0)
                      }
                      \\mathbb{R}^{9,1}
                      \\,.
            %li
              %p
                A closed
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+0-form"} differential 0-form
                (the “
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/massive+type+IIA+supergravity"}> Romans mass
                ”)
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi F
                        %mn 0
                      %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                      %mo ∈
                      %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                      %msubsup
                        %mi Ω
                        %mi dR
                        %mn 0
                      %mo{:maxsize => "1.8em", :minsize => "1.8em"} (
                      %msup
                        %mi ℝ
                        %mrow
                          %mn 9
                          %mo ,
                          %mn 1
                      %mo ∖
                      %msup
                        %mi ℝ
                        %mrow
                          %mn 8
                          %mo ,
                          %mn 1
                      %mo{:maxsize => "1.8em", :minsize => "1.8em"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                      F_0
                      \\,\in\,
                      \\Omega^0_{dR}
                      \\Big(
                      \\mathbb{R}^{9,1}
                      \\setminus
                      \\mathbb{R}^{8,1}
                      \\Big)
              %p
                being the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/RR-field"} RR-field
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/flux+density"} flux density
                sourced by a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D8-brane"} D8-brane
                whose worldvolume
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi ℝ
                        %mrow
                          %mn 1
                          %mo ,
                          %mn 8
                      %mover
                        %mo ↪
                        %mrow
                          %mover
                            %mi x
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} →
                          %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                          %mo ↦
                          %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mover
                            %mi x
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} →
                          %mo ,
                          %mi d
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %msup
                        %mi ℝ
                        %mrow
                          %mn 1
                          %mo ,
                          %mn 9
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                      \\mathbb{R}^{1,8}
                      \\overset{
                      \\vec x \,\mapsto\, (\vec x, d)
                      }{
                      \\hookrightarrow
                      }
                      \\mathbb{R}^{1,9}
              %p
                we take to be located at
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi x
                        %mn 9
                      %mo =
                      %mi d
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x^9=d
                for some
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi d
                        %mo ∈
                        %msub
                          %mi ℝ
                          %mo +
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d \in \mathbb{R}_+
            %li
              %p
                A
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+2-form"} differential 2-form
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi F
                        %mn 2
                      %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                      %mo ∈
                      %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                      %msubsup
                        %mi Ω
                        %mi dR
                        %mn 3
                      %mo{:maxsize => "1.8em", :minsize => "1.8em"} (
                      %msup
                        %mi ℝ
                        %mrow
                          %mn 9
                          %mo ,
                          %mn 1
                      %mo ∖
                      %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                      %msup
                        %mi ℝ
                        %mrow
                          %mn 5
                          %mo ,
                          %mn 1
                      %mo ∪
                      %msup
                        %mi ℝ
                        %mrow
                          %mn 6
                          %mo ,
                          %mn 1
                      %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                      %mo{:maxsize => "1.8em", :minsize => "1.8em"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                      F_2
                      \\,\in\,
                      \\Omega^3_{dR}
                      \\Big(
                      \\mathbb{R}^{9,1}
                      \\setminus
                      \\big(
                      \\mathbb{R}^{5,1}
                      \\cup
                      \\mathbb{R}^{6,1}
                      \\big)
                      \\Big)
              %p
                being the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/RR-field"} RR-field
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/flux+density"} flux density
                sourced by a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D6-brane"} D6-brane
                with
                %em potential worldvolume
                (“potential” because the D6 may have
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo ∼
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sim
                vanishing charge carried by parts of its worldvolume, hence may “disappear” from its would-be worldvolume locus in parts, as we will see):
              #eq:D6BraneWorldvolume.maruku-equation
                %span.maruku-eq-number (2)
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi ℝ
                        %mrow
                          %mn 6
                          %mo ,
                          %mn 1
                      %mover
                        %mo ↪
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %msup
                            %mi x
                            %mn 0
                          %mo ,
                          %mover
                            %mi x
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} →
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                          %mo ↦
                          %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                          %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                          %msup
                            %mi x
                            %mn 0
                          %mo ,
                          %mover
                            %mn 0
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} →
                          %mo ,
                          %mover
                            %mi x
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} →
                          %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                      %msup
                        %mi ℝ
                        %mrow
                          %mn 9
                          %mo ,
                          %mn 1
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                      \\mathbb{R}^{6,1}
                      \\xhookrightarrow{
                      (x^0, \vec x)
                      \\,\mapsto\,
                      \\big(x^0, \vec 0, \vec x\big)
                      }
                      \\mathbb{R}^{9,1}
              %p transverse to that of both the NS5-brane and the D8-brane and satisying the equation
              #eq:BianchiIdentityForD6BraneFlux.maruku-equation
                %span.maruku-eq-number (3)
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} d
                      %msub
                        %mi F
                        %mn 2
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mo =
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %msub
                        %mi H
                        %mn 3
                      %mo ∧
                      %msub
                        %mi F
                        %mn 0
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mo ∈
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %msubsup
                        %mi Ω
                        %mi dR
                        %mn 3
                      %mo{:maxsize => "1.8em", :minsize => "1.8em"} (
                      %msup
                        %mi ℝ
                        %mrow
                          %mn 9
                          %mo ,
                          %mn 1
                      %mo ∖
                      %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                      %msup
                        %mi ℝ
                        %mrow
                          %mn 5
                          %mo ,
                          %mn 1
                      %mo ∪
                      %msup
                        %mi ℝ
                        %mrow
                          %mn 8
                          %mo ,
                          %mn 1
                      %mo ∪
                      %msup
                        %mi ℝ
                        %mrow
                          %mn 6
                          %mo ,
                          %mn 1
                      %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                      %mo{:maxsize => "1.8em", :minsize => "1.8em"} )
                      %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                      %mo ,
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                      \\mathrm{d}
                      F_{2}
                      \\;=\;
                      H_3 \wedge F_{0}
                      \\;\;\;\;\;
                      \\in
                      \\;
                      \\Omega^3_{dR}
                      \\Big(
                      \\mathbb{R}^{9,1}
                      \\setminus
                      \\big(
                      \\mathbb{R}^{5,1}
                      \\cup
                      \\mathbb{R}^{8,1}
                      \\cup
                      \\mathbb{R}^{6,1}
                      \\big)
                      \\Big)
                      \\,,
              %p
                where now
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi H
                        %mn 3
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H_3
                and
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi F
                        %mn 0
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F_0
                are understood of the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pullback+of+differential+forms"} pullback
                (restriction) of the above
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+forms"} differential forms
                of these names to the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complement"} complement
                of the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D6-brane"} D6-brane
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/worldvolume"} worldvolume
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.maruku-eqref{:href => "#eq:D6BraneWorldvolume"} (2)
              %p
                Notice that even if/though the original forms
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi H
                        %mn 3
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H_3
                is
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    not
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/exact+differential+form"} exact
                %a.maruku-eqref{:href => "#eq:BianchiIdentityForD6BraneFlux"} (3)
                is meaningful.
          %p In order to model the Hanany-Witten effect proper as considered by previous authors, we declare the following boundary conditions:
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                The
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/massive+type+IIA+supergravity"} Romans vacuum
                is to the “right” of the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D8-brane"} D8-brane
              #eq:RomansVacuum.maruku-equation
                %span.maruku-eq-number (4)
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi x
                        %mn 9
                      %mo &gt;
                      %mi d
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
